From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:14:04 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 122/202] Meridian: on Windows, no title bar and one bar across
 the top, as Arc has there

The browser window on Windows had Windows's own title bar above the UI
page. It has none now (webui_browser_frame_view_win.cc: a frame that draws
nothing, leaves the whole window to the page and answers the hit tests for
resizing), like the macOS window under its transparent title bar.

In its place the UI page has a bar across the top on Windows: a menu and
Hide Sidebar on the left, Back, Forward and Reload at the sidebar's edge,
the URL pill in the middle, and the caption buttons on the right. The bar
is what the window is dragged by. The controls and the pill are the same
elements as everywhere else: the page moves them from the sidebar into the
bar when it starts on Windows, so nothing about them differs on macOS,
where the bar stays hidden and unused.

The menu holds what the menu bar has on macOS and no button has: New Tab,
Folder and Space, Ask, Chat, Workbench, Mission Control, Archive, Downloads,
Import from Arc, Welcome Tour, Settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
